Phase 7 Task 7.1 (bead VieNeuTTSApp-nqx.9.1) — the frozen host ships the
lightweight half of the Qwen engine and nothing of the model stack.

Delivered:
- Frozen re-dispatch (`core/qwen_engine.py`, `__main__.py`): `host_command()`
  is now platform-aware — a source checkout still runs
  `[python, -m, vienetts_app.workers.qwen_host]`, while a PyInstaller build
  (`sys.frozen`) re-dispatches ITSELF as `[<exe>, --qwen-host]`, because a
  frozen app has no separate interpreter to hand a module name to. The CLI
  routes `--qwen-host` to the host half BEFORE the GUI import and before
  `ensure_windowed_stdio()`: stdout is the frame channel, so the windowed-exe
  stdio safety net must never touch it. The flag is deliberately not in
  argparse's surface (internal contract, not a user option).
- Runtime import path (`workers/qwen_host.py`, `host_environment()`): the host
  now owns its import path. The parent passes the managed runtime's
  site-packages in `VIENETTS_QWEN_RUNTIME` and `configure_import_path()`
  inserts it at `sys.path[0]` before the first heavy import, because a frozen
  host cannot rely on PYTHONPATH (PyInstaller's importer ignores it). The
  runtime-only imports stay deferred, so the bundle carries no torch.
- Windowless Windows: the `os.name == "nt"` branch in `_spawn` became the
  patchable `IS_WINDOWS` seam (patching `os.name` breaks pathlib) and is
  asserted to pass `CREATE_NO_WINDOW`, with the spec's `console=False` as the
  other half of the contract.
- Spec (`packaging/vienetts-app.spec`): excludes now cover the whole
  Qwen-runtime-only stack (`torch`, `torchaudio`, `transformers`, `qwen_tts`,
  `accelerate`, `einops`, `safetensors`, `sox`) with the rationale in the
  header; the host and protocol modules are explicit hidden imports; the QML
  and asset trees stay inside `vienetts_app/` (the layout app.py resolves
  against). No runtime, wheel or weight is ever collected.
- Release pipeline (`.github/workflows/release.yml`): two new post-build
  steps — the bundle is asserted free of the Qwen/PyTorch stack (find over
  `dist/`, failing loudly when `dist/` is missing), and the packaged binary is
  probed with `--qwen-host` (no runtime, no models): it must exit 0, log
  `starting` and emit its hello frame through the real protocol reader. Both
  were dry-run locally against a wrapper binary and against clean/dirty/missing
  dist trees.

Tests: tests/unit/test_package.py grew from 1 to 17 cases — frozen
`host_command` re-dispatch, CLI routing (host flag before the GUI stdio setup;
GUI dispatch still works without it), the runtime env entry, a real subprocess
that proves `configure_import_path()` inserts a path with spaces and non-ASCII
characters, a real host start from that path (hello frame, `starting` →
